    "description": "• USB technology expert and USB-IF contributor\n• Architect, lead implementor, and key maintainer for Apple’s unified USB host stack, encompassing support of standards-based hardware and proprietary extensions for Apple Silicon and third-party hardware\n• Work closely with silicon engineering teams to investigate, root cause, and evaluate software solutions to hardware issues\n• Participate in silicon specification reviews and provide input on features and fixes desired for future products\n• Developed and maintain internal tooling to enable automated triage of incoming problem reports and more efficient evaluation of system panic reports\n• Extensive experience investigating and resolving USB issues for both hosts and devices, including cross-functional collaboration\n\nDesigned, implemented, and maintain:\n• Transport-agnostic virtual host controller to enable new features and product lines\n• User-mode host controller interface to facilitate system security goals and enable new use cases for third-party developers\n• Drivers for the unified high-speed PHY for external I/O\n• System-critical USB function drivers",
